# Fathom Analytics

> Fathom Analytics is a simple, privacy-focused website analytics tool. It's a Google Analytics alternative that doesn't compromise visitor privacy.

## Help Documentation

### Getting Started

- [Ad and email campaigns (UTMs)](https://usefathom.com/docs/start/utms): Suppose you want to collect data for digital campaigns, ad clicks, campaigns on social media, or even newsletter/email campaigns.
- [Create a Fathom account](https://usefathom.com/docs/start/create): Fathom Analytics is a hosted website analytics software tool.
- [Dashboard explained](https://usefathom.com/docs/start/dashboard): First, let's start with what Fathom Analytics is: simple, GDPR-compliant website analytics that shows you data about your website on a dashboard or email report.
- [Do I need to sign the DPA?](https://usefathom.com/docs/start/dpa): We can’t offer legal advice, but we can talk about the purpose of our DPA. 
- [How do free trials work?](https://usefathom.com/docs/start/trials): When you sign up for an account with Fathom Analytics, you get a 7-day free trial.
- [Our sample privacy policy](https://usefathom.com/docs/start/policy): Since our software is privacy-first website analytics, there’s typically less to do on your end because we collect such a minimal amount of data from visitors.
- [How Fathom measures your analytics](https://usefathom.com/docs/start/measurement): A complete guide to how every metric on your Fathom dashboard is calculated, how attribution works, and what the numbers mean.
- [Script installation](https://usefathom.com/docs/start/install): To start collecting data from your website, you need to install our script in the header of your site’s code.
- [Using keyboard shortcuts](https://usefathom.com/docs/start/shortcuts): Fathom Analytics has keyboard shortcuts for navigating your dashboard quickly.

### How-tos

- [Compare two date ranges](https://usefathom.com/docs/how-tos/compare-dates): Turn on comparison mode to see how this period stacks up against the previous one, last month, last year, or a custom range.
- [Measure a marketing campaign](https://usefathom.com/docs/how-tos/measure-a-campaign): Tag your campaign links with UTMs, then filter your dashboard (and save a view) to see traffic and conversions from that campaign.
- [Switch from Google Analytics](https://usefathom.com/docs/how-tos/switch-from-google-analytics): Install Fathom alongside Google Analytics, import your history, then remove GA when you're happy with the data.
- [Track Google Ads](https://usefathom.com/docs/how-tos/track-google-ads): See which Google Ads campaigns send visits and events to your Fathom dashboard, using UTMs. No Google tag needed.

### Script & Installation

- [Add the embed script](https://usefathom.com/docs/script/embed): To start using Fathom Analytics, you simply have to add a single line of code to the head section of your website
- [Advanced embed script settings](https://usefathom.com/docs/script/script-advanced): These are the advanced options we offer with our embed script.
- [Blocking local/test environments](https://usefathom.com/docs/script/local): How to keep Fathom from collecting analytics data from local, staging, and test environments.
- [EU isolation](https://usefathom.com/docs/script/eu-isolation): If you want to use EU isolation, congratulations; as a Fathom customer, you’re already using it, and it’s enabled by default!
- [Exclude your own visits](https://usefathom.com/docs/script/exclude-visits): There are two ways to block your visits from showing up in your analytics with Fathom.
- [Multiple site IDs with one website](https://usefathom.com/docs/script/multiple-site-ids-one-website): Sending visit data to multiple dashboards from one website
- [Site firewall settings](https://usefathom.com/docs/script/firewall): Block or allow pages, IPs, referrers, domains, countries, and event names from the firewall settings on your site.

### Events & Conversions

- [Creating and using events](https://usefathom.com/docs/events/overview): Events (or goals) in Fathom are things you want to collect data about, which aren’t just page views.
- [Track 404/error pages](https://usefathom.com/docs/events/404-page-tracking): Track visits to missing pages with Fathom events so you can find broken links and add redirects.
- [Track ecommerce conversions](https://usefathom.com/docs/events/ecommerce-conversions): Track ecommerce conversions, event values and currencies in Fathom Analytics.
- [Track external link clicks](https://usefathom.com/docs/events/external-clicks): Track outbound link clicks as events in Fathom Analytics, for individual links or all external links.
- [Track form submissions](https://usefathom.com/docs/events/form-submission-tracking): Track successful form submissions as conversions with Fathom Analytics events.
- [Track link clicks](https://usefathom.com/docs/events/link-clicks): Track link clicks with Fathom Analytics using an onclick handler or a JavaScript event listener.
- [Track page load conversions](https://usefathom.com/docs/events/page-load-conversions): Record a Fathom event when an important page loads to measure page load conversions.

### Features

- [All sites view](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/all-sites): When you click on your site name from the dashboard, you’ll see an ‘All sites’ link at the bottom of the dropdown.
- [API](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/api): Use the Fathom Analytics API to manage sites, events and milestones, or pull custom reports.
- [Bot detection](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/bot-detection): How Fathom detects and blocks bot traffic to keep your analytics accurate.
- [Email reports](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/email-reports): Email reports are a time-saving way to get a snapshot of your analytics right in your inbox.
- [Export your data](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/exporting): Your website analytics are yours, so you can download your data whenever you'd like.
- [Filtering and searching](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/filtering): You can add a filter by clicking on any row on your dashboard.
- [Google Analytics Importer](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/ga-importer): It's easy to import your data from Google Analytics (GA4) into your Fathom dashboard.
- [Milestones](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/milestones): Milestones let you mark important events directly on your chart, so you can quickly understand what might have caused changes in your traffic.
- [Multi-domains](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/multi): Say you have several domains (and subdomains) and want to collect data for all of them on a single Fathom dashboard.
- [Saved views](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/saved-views): Save a combination of filters as a named view and switch back to it in one click.
- [Search Console integration](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/google-search-console): See which search terms people use to find your site in search results, right inside your Fathom dashboard.
- [Share a dashboard](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/shared-dashboards): Give clients, contractors and colleagues their own link to your Fathom dashboard, with an optional password and expiry date.
- [Data removals](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/data-removals): Remove unwanted visits, such as test runs, staging traffic or spam, from your past data. You can undo a removal at any time.
- [Traffic sources](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/sources): The Sources tab, in the Referrals box, divides your content into a few buckets based on where the traffic came from, which you can then filter.
- [UTMs and campaigns](https://usefathom.com/docs/features/campaigns): A UTM parameter is the text included in the URL to understand where the traffic is coming from.

