### Troubleshooting

- [Can I add more than 50 sites?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/sites): Every plan includes at least 50 sites. Bigger plans include more, and you can add extra packs yourself.
- [Do I lose my stats if I change a URL or site name?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/changing): Learn what happens to your Fathom Analytics stats and tracking code when you change your website URL or rename a site in your account.
- [Does Fathom have “X” feature?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/features): Find the features available in Fathom Analytics and see recently released improvements in our changelog.
- [Does Fathom use cookies or require a consent banner?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/cookies): It may be hard to “fathom” (sorry, bad joke), but Fathom Analytics doesn’t use cookies or similar technologies in our analytics.
- [Does replacing Google Analytics hurt my SEO?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/seo): No. Your site will not be negatively impacted if you use Fathom Analytics instead of Google Analytics.
- [How do I transfer a dashboard to another account?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/transfer): You can transfer a site (dashboard) to another Fathom account yourself from the site’s Manage settings.
- [How to get CookieBot to Ignore Fathom](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/cookiebot): CookieBot incorrectly assumes Fathom Analytics needs to have consent - here’s how to avoid this
- [If Fathom isn't working on your site](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/not-working): If you believe you have added our embed script correctly and no visits are showing up, there’s a problem with your configuration.
- [Only my homepage is showing up in my data](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/canonicals): This typically happens if you’ve only added our embed script to your homepage (and not into the header of your site template).
- [See Google search terms (keywords)](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/google-keywords): Since 2011 all search traffic from Google has been encrypted, meaning you have to use Google Search Console to view it
- [What are salts and hashes?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/hashes-salts): Understand hashes and salts, how they differ from encryption, and their role in privacy-focused website analytics.
- [Why am I not seeing the full referrer URL?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/referrer-policy): Explanation on why customers sometimes only see the referrer domain without the pathname included
- [Why am I seeing duplicate pathnames in my data?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/duplicate-pathnames): Learn why you may see duplicate page paths in your Fathom dashboard and how to fix them.
- [Why am I seeing UTM parameters I didn't make?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/utm): Since we launched UTM parameters in the dashboard, we’ve had a few questions from customers who may see UTM data they didn’t create.
- [Why are my stats different from other analytics?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/differences): If you compare Fathom to another analytics platform, the stats will undoubtedly vary.
- [Why is Fathom better than European-only providers?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/eu-only): “EU-only analytics” can also slow down your analytics for people not in the EU.
- [Why is my account locked?](https://usefathom.com/docs/troubleshooting/locked): Find out why your Fathom Analytics account is locked and how to resolve unpaid invoices or upgrade a plan that no longer fits your traffic.

